L(1,chi): fake gives e^gamma (log log^2 q + log c + I1), I1 = int a dv over v>0 = -0.7265
   log c + I1 = -1.0013  vs LLS Thm 1.5 ceiling 1 - 2 log 2 = -0.3863  -> satisfied
   (if chi(p) were 0-mean right above X, L(1) alone would force c <= e/4 = 0.6796)
phase at t=0: G(0) = 1.14731 > 0  => rho(0) = -G/M = -1: zero clusters at t = +-pi/L, +-3pi/L, ... (L = log X ~ 2 loglog q)
   cluster size  = log q / L          = (1/2) log q/loglog q   [= Goldston-Gonek multiplicity ceiling]
   S(t) sawtooth = +-(1/2) cluster    = (1/4) log q/loglog q   [= Carneiro-Chandee-Milinovich ceiling]
   lowest zero   = pi/L               = (pi/2)/loglog q,  gap = pi/loglog q  [= known gap ceiling]
   |L(1/2+it)| between clusters ~ 2^(log q/L) = exp((log2/2) log q/loglog q)  [= Chandee-Soundararajan ceiling]
